--- field object.network.id
type: str
asserted: true

The Registry network record identifier whose Connect descriptor radiusd checked.

Copied from radiusd's audit context by the kernel. The object kind is `network`;
its access mask defines Connect as bit 0 (0x1). This is a configuration identity,
not a kernel-observed network or proof that the supplied descriptor belongs to it.

--- field object.network.ssid
type: str
asserted: true

The network's SSID as a display label, copied from radiusd's audit context.

Invalid UTF-8 bytes are replaced with U+FFFD for display. This label never
selects policy; radiusd binds the exchange using the original SSID bytes and
identifies the configuration with `object.network.id`.

--- field source.radiusd.username
type: str

The inner PAP username supplied by the peer, before identity verification.

This is unverified input, including on success. It is not a SID or proof of
identity. It can contain a typing mistake or arbitrary peer-controlled text.

--- field object.radiusd.canonical-name
type: str

The canonical account name returned by authd after password verification.

--- field object.radiusd.attempt.guid
type: bin.guid

The random identifier of the short-lived authentication conversation.

--- field object.radiusd.client.id
type: uint

The first eight bytes of SHA-256 of the client record name, as a big-endian integer.

This identifies configuration, not an AP's asserted NAS identity.

--- field object.radiusd.network.id
type: uint

The first eight bytes of SHA-256 of the network record name, as a big-endian integer.

--- event radiusd.exchange.attempted
tier: standard
gating: integrity-checked exchanges allocated a server conversation
cardinality: once when the logical conversation terminates; retransmissions write none

A RADIUS authentication conversation ended.

Success means that current network policy granted Connect and the UDP socket
accepted the Access-Accept for transmission. It does not prove that the AP
received it or admitted a device. Timeout and binding invalidation also end
conversations. Invalid initial datagrams and requests rejected before state
allocation write none. Reporting failure does not change admission.

This operational event is not a kernel access-audit record and does not
satisfy SACL audit requirements. It contains no password, shared secret,
private key, raw credential packet, or disclosed claim values.

field: subject.token.sid                    required
  The radiusd service account emitting the event, not the Wi-Fi user.
field: source.radiusd.username              optional
  Present after a valid UTF-8 inner username reaches credential verification.
field: object.radiusd.attempt.guid          required
field: object.radiusd.client.id             required
field: object.radiusd.network.id            required
field: object.radiusd.canonical-name        optional
  Present only after authd verified the password, including later denials.
field: object.account.sid                   optional
  Present together with the canonical name; the verified user's SID.
field: outcome.success                      required
field: outcome.reason                       when outcome.success == false
  values: authentication-failed | permission-denied | missing-context | authority-unavailable | kernel-api-unavailable | access-check-error | conversation-limit | timed-out | binding-changed | protocol-error | undelivered | allowance-exhausted | accounting-unavailable
  closed: false

--- event radiusd.configuration.loaded
tier: standard
gating: startup and observed configuration changes or transitions to unavailable
cardinality: once per validated activation or observed transition to invalid configuration

The service activated configuration or paused admissions because it could not.

An activation validates Registry configuration copied from one read-only
snapshot, then separately loads its referenced credential files. A failure
retains old sockets and bounded conversations but blocks new admissions and
cached success replies until validation recovers.

field: subject.token.sid                    required
field: config.root                          required
  Always Machine\Software\Radius.
field: outcome.success                      required
field: outcome.reason                       when outcome.success == false
  values: invalid-or-unavailable
  closed: false

--- event radiusd.accounting.health.changed
tier: standard
gating: accounting health observed at five-second intervals
cardinality: once on the first observation and each observed health transition

Accounting availability changed.

Success means accounting is off or its validated listeners and ledger are
available. It does not establish that a device delivered every report.
Failure covers invalid configuration, unavailable listeners, and storage
failures. Inspect the protected local accounting status for diagnostics.

The event contains the service actor and health outcome only. Personal
accounting history, identifiers, addresses, and usage remain in the protected
ledger. Rebuild does not replay this event. Submission is best effort.

field: subject.token.sid                    required
  The radiusd service account, never a network user's SID.
field: outcome.success                      required
